#: ../../site/guides/metrics.md:1
msgid "Metrics and rolling windows"
msgstr "指标与滚动窗口"

#: ../../site/guides/metrics.md:3
msgid ""
"This guide explains how the metric families fit together, which conventions "
"the numbers follow, and what each family returns when the input is "
"degenerate. It is a map, not a substitute for the API reference: every "
"function carries the exact formula and failure rule in its own "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"本指南说明各指标族之间的关系、数值遵循的约定，以及输入退化时每个族返回什么。它是地图，不能替代 API "
"参考：每个函数的确切公式与失败规则都写在它自己的文档里。"

#: ../../site/guides/metrics.md:8
msgid "Inputs and units"
msgstr "输入与单位"

#: ../../site/guides/metrics.md:10
msgid ""
"Metric functions take a `fincore::dataframe`, a column name (defaulting to "
"`\"returns\"` for most of them) and, where relevant, a risk-free rate. "
"Values are decimal returns (`0.01` is one percent). Timestamps are UTC "
"nanosecond instants and are used for ordering, window boundaries and date-"
"based grouping, not for arithmetic on the values."
msgstr ""
"指标函数接受 `fincore::dataframe`、列名（多数函数默认 "
"`\"returns\"`）以及（在相关时）无风险利率。数值是小数收益（`0.01` 表示 1%）。时间戳是 UTC "
"纳秒时刻，用于排序、窗口边界与按日期分组，而不是对数值做算术。"

#: ../../site/guides/metrics.md:16
msgid ""
"`NaN` means \"missing\" everywhere in this library. It is not silently "
"replaced by zero, and it is not dropped from a frame. Each function states "
"whether it drops missing observations pairwise, per column or not at all; "
"the default for the scalar ratios is to drop `NaN` and work with the "
"remaining values."
msgstr ""
"`NaN` 在本库中到处表示“缺失”。它不会被静默替换为 "
"0，也不会被从帧中删掉。每个函数都会说明它是按配对、按列还是完全不丢弃缺失观测；标量比率的默认做法是丢弃 `NaN` 并用剩下的值计算。"

#: ../../site/guides/metrics.md:21
msgid ""
"An empty or mis-typed column is a structural error and raises `input_error`."
" A column that exists but is too short usually yields `NaN` rather than an "
"exception, because \"not enough data\" is a value, not a programming "
"mistake."
msgstr "空列或类型不符的列是结构性错误，会抛 `input_error`。列存在但过短通常返回 `NaN` 而不是异常，因为“数据不足”是一个值，不是编程错误。"

